2026-08-25T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2028) '### entities/: the objects, and the interactors that act on them
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2028) 'An entity is an object the component works on, and it knows nothing
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2028) 'about where it is stored. An interactor performs the actions on
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2028) 'entities. Together they open no socket, read no device, and link no
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2028) 'framework. They carry their own `entities/spec/` of tests that run in
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2028) 'isolation against recorded data. A transport layer never reaches
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2028) 'inside them.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2028) '### repositories/: interfaces to the entities
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A repository is an interface that gets, creates, and changes entities.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2028) 'The interactor declares it and a data source implements it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A repository stays at the lowest common denominator every binding
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2028) 'language can implement: a C-ABI struct of function pointers where a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2028) 'service crosses languages, a language-native interface where it does
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2028) 'not. One header then binds C, C++, and Python data sources alike.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2028) '### datasources/: the implementations, outside the interactor
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A data source implements a repository against the real world: a serial
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2028) 'device, a UDP socket, a recorded fixture for CI, a GPU compute host, a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2028) 'renderer, an engine runtime. One repository admits many data sources,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2028) 'so one pass of an interactor reaches several destinations, and a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2028) 'recorded fixture stands in for live hardware under CI.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2028) '### The transport layer, and composition across the seam
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2028) 'A transport layer is the input that triggers an interactor. All
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2028) 'dependencies point inward, so the transport layer depends on the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2028) 'interactor and never the reverse.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Components compose when a data source of one component is the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2028) 'transport layer of another. An in-process dependency links the sibling
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2028) 'directly. A cross-process dependency meets on a wire, which is a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2028) 'protocol the two ends share. The wire is the integration contract, so
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2028) 'a producer in one language and a consumer in another share no code,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2028) 'only the message format. Each component declares its sibling wiring
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2028) 'beside its repositories.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2028) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2028) '- Entities and interactors with no dependencies let CI replay recorded
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2028) '  data through them with no device and no runtime.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2028) '- The wire seam decouples languages and processes, so any component is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2028) '  rewritable or replaceable as long as it keeps the message contract.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2028) '- A new output is a new data source, with no change to the interactor
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2028) '  that produced the data.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-2028) '- All dependencies point inward, so a data source depends on the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-2028) '  interactor through a repository, and the interactor depends on
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:35Z (RFD66606-2028) '  nothing.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:36Z (RFD66606-2028) '- The convention costs interface boilerplate, and across a process
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:37Z (RFD66606-2028) '  boundary it adds a serialize and parse step the in-process link
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:38Z (RFD66606-2028) '  avoids. That cost buys cross-language, cross-process composition.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:39Z (RFD66606-2028) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2028  1 LINE
 Text:Written

